"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-023317","Abbreviation_in_the_article":1,"Cell_line":"HEK293","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":">30","IC50_Dark_value":30,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/smll.202405771","Year":2025,"Counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-023318","Abbreviation_in_the_article":1,"Cell_line":"HUVEC","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":">30","IC50_Dark_value":30,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/smll.202405771","Year":2025,"Counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":1,"value":1.65,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1002/smll.202405771","year":2025,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-003954","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The octanol/water partition coefficient (Log P), is calculated based on the equation (1): Log P = Log(Coctanol / Cwater). The partition coefficient of complexes 1–7 were determined through the shake-flask method. To prepare water-saturated octanol, 4 mL of octanol was mixed with 1 ml of water and left for 24 h. Similarly, octanol-saturated water was prepared using the same procedure. The complex (50 μM) was then solubilized in 2 mL of saturated water by adding a minimal volume of DMSO, and this solution was added to 2 mL of saturated octanol. The resulting mixture underwent 24 h of shaking using a mechanical shaker, followed by settling and separation. The concentration of the complex was subsequently assessed through UV-vis absorption spectroscopy."}]}